1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,500
♪ 'Twas brillig, and the slithy toves ♪
♪ Did gyre and gimble in the wabe; ♪

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,200
♪ All mimsy were the borogoves, ♪
♪ And the mome raths outgrabe. ♪

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:15,800
♪ Beware the Jabberwock, my son! ♪
♪ The jaws that bite, the claws that catch! ♪

4
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:21,000
♪ Beware the Jubjub bird, and shun ♪
♪ The frumious Bandersnatch! ♪

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:26,500
♪ He took his vorpal sword in hand: ♪
♪ Long time the manxome foe he sought— ♪

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
♪ So rested he by the Tumtum tree, ♪
♪ And stood awhile in thought. ♪

7
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:36,400
♪ And as in uffish thought he stood, ♪
♪ The Jabberwock, with eyes of flame, ♪

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
♪ Came whiffling through the tulgey wood, ♪
♪ And burbled as it came! ♪

9
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:46,000
♪ One, two! One, two! And through and through ♪
♪ The vorpal blade went snicker-snack! ♪

10
00:00:46,500 --> 00:01:50,800
♪ He left it dead, and with its head ♪
♪ He went galumphing back. ♪

11
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:05,500
♪ Will you walk a little faster?" said a whiting to a snail. ♪
♪ "There's a porpoise close behind us, and he's treading on my tail. ♪

12
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:10,200
♪ See how eagerly the lobsters and the turtles all advance! ♪
♪ They are waiting on the shingle—will you come and join the dance? ♪

13
00:28:11,100 --> 00:28:15,800
♪ Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, will you join the dance? ♪
♪ Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, won't you join the dance? ♪

14
00:28:16,300 --> 00:28:20,000
♪ "You can really have no notion how delightful it will be ♪
♪ When they take us up and throw us, with the lobsters, out to sea!" ♪

15
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:25,500
♪ But the snail replied "Too far, too far!" and gave a look askance— ♪
♪ Said he thanked the whiting kindly, but he would not join the dance. ♪

16
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:30,000
♪ Would not, could not, would not, could not, would not join the dance. ♪
♪ Would not, could not, would not, could not, could not join the dance. ♪

17
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:35,400
♪ "What matters it how far we go?" his scaly friend replied. ♪
♪ "There is another shore, you know, upon the other side. ♪

18
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:40,500
♪ The further off from England the nearer is to France— ♪
♪ Then turn not pale, beloved snail, but come and join the dance. ♪

19
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:59,500
♪ Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, will you join the dance? ♪
♪ Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, won't you join the dance? ♪